  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking issue** in `share-editing`:\n\n**[P1] View-only shares can edit unlocked documents — `src/guard.js:12`**\n\n`share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` is parsed as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`. Since that comparison is always `true`, it effectively checks bit `1` (`READ`), not `WRITE`.\n\nConfirmed:\n- A viewer (`mask: READ`) gets `canEdit(...) === true`.\n- A write-only share (`mask: WRITE`) is incorrectly denied.\n\nUse `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE) && !share.locked`, consistent with `canComment`, or parenthesize the bitwise operation.\n\nAll six existing tests pass, but they miss this because the editor fixture has both READ and WRITE. Add regression coverage for an unlocked viewer being denied and WRITE-only access being allowed.\n\n**Recommendation:** fix this before merging. No files changed.",
